 695               /THIS SUBROUTINE TAKES THE INVERSE FFT (IFFT) OF THE DATA IN THE BUFFER.
 696               /IT IS ASSUMED THAT THIS DATA IS STORED IN SEQUENTIAL ORDER.
 697               /THE RESULTS ARE STORED IN BIT INVERTED ORDER.
 698               /THE ALGORITHM USED IS AS FOLLOWS:
 699               /       THE NORMAL TRANSFORM IS PERFORMED, EXCEPT:
 700               /       ON FETCHING THE VALUE FOR IM[W^K], WHICH IS 
 701               /       THE SIN(2*PI*K/N), THIS SIN VALUE IS NEGATED.
 702               /
 703               /THE REASONING FOR THIS IS AS FOLLOWS:
 704               /       A WEIGHTING FACTOR OF W^(-K) IS USED IN THE IFFT
 705               /       AND SINCE W^K AND W^(-K) ARE THE SAME EXCEPT THAT
 706               /       THEIR IMAGINARY PARTS HAVE OPPOSITE SIGNS, IT FOLLOWS
 707               /       THAT IM[W^K] SHOULD BE REPLACED BY -IM[W^K].
